{"name":"London Calling","hex":"#cdcccf","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"calling","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of call"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A strong urge (to do some particular thing with or in one's life, for example to become religious, to help the poor, or to be an entertainer).","A job or occupation."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/calling"}],"entries":[{"title":"London Calling","blocks":[{"text":"London Calling is the third studio album by the English rock band the Clash. It was originally released as a double album in the United Kingdom on 14 December 1979 by CBS Records, and in the United States and Canada in January 1980 by Epic Records."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/00/TheClashLondonCallingalbumcover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/London_Calling","wikidata":"Q19003"},{"title":"London Calling (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"London Calling\" is a song by the English rock band the Clash. It was released as a single from the band's 1979 double album of the same name. This apocalyptic, politically charged rant features the band's post-punk sound, electric guitar and vocals."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f7/The_Clash_-_London_Calling.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/London_Calling_(song)","wikidata":"Q644416"},{"title":"London","blocks":[{"text":"London is the capital and largest city of England and the United Kingdom, with a population of 9.14 million people in 2025. Its wider metropolitan area is the largest in Western Europe, with a population of 15.4 million. London stands on the River Thames in southeast England, at the head of a 50-mile (80 km) tidal estuary down to the North Sea, and has been a major settlement for nearly 2,000 years. Its ancient core and financial centre, the City of London, was founded by the Romans as Londinium and has retained its medieval boundaries. The City of Westminster, to the west of the City of London, has been the site of the national government and parliament for centuries. London grew rapidly in the 19th century, becoming the world's largest city at the time. Since the 19th century the name \"London\" has referred to the metropolis around the City of London, historically split among the counties of Middlesex, Essex, Surrey, Kent and Hertfordshire. Since 1965 it has largely comprised the administrative area of Greater London, governed by 33 local authorities and the Greater London Authority."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/London_Skyline_%28125508655%29.jpeg/330px-London_Skyline_%28125508655%29.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/London","wikidata":"Q84"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/JoeStrummer1980.jpg/500px-JoeStrummer1980.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/JoeStrummer1980.jpg/1280px-JoeStrummer1980.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/JoeStrummer1980.jpg/500px-JoeStrummer1980.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJoeStrummer1980.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/MickJones1980.jpg/500px-MickJones1980.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/MickJones1980.jpg/1280px-MickJones1980.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimed